\f1\fs22 \'93Fortunately, Shakti\'92s dental plan is first rate.\'94\
Sarah took her time. \'93You seemed to be alarmed about the self-tuning feature of the whole thing. Will it not prevent the kinds of instability that were so problematic in previous attempts?\'94\
\'93It will allow everything to run much smoother.\'94 Chip sounded like a judge handing down a life sentence. \'93And that\'92s a problem.\'94\
\'93What\'97\'94\
\'93I should tender my resignation, Ms Jacobson.\'94\
Sarah studied the hulking man in the front seat with her. \'93Fine. You can take it to Eloise personally. I\'92m sure she\'92ll wish you all the best and throw you a party.\'94\
Chip\'92s shoulders rounded. \'93I should, but it won\'92t do me any good. I\'92m trapped here\'97for more reasons that just Eloise.\'94\
\'93I know how that feels,\'94 Sarah conceded. \'93I thought the stuff about rubber geometry\'97\'94\
\'93Rubber topology,\'94 Chip corrected.\
Sarah accepted the correction with a nod. \'93So you are familiar with it.\'94\
\'93It\'92s cute talking about triangles on a two dimensional plane,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93Sure, but the discs move in three dimensions.\'94\
Chip said nothing and Sarah read the pause. She waited Chip out; she waited for him to realise she was figuring it out.\
Chip eventually filled the gap. \'93Gyges discs spin in 
\f2\i all
\f1\i0  the dimensions.\'94\
\'93What does that mean?\'97All the dimensions.\'94\
\'93In the mathematical formulae the symbol 
\f2\i G
\f1\i0 , means 
\f2\i all the dimensions.
\f1\i0 \'94\
\'93Huh,\'94 Sarah thought. \'93I would\'92ve thought that 
\f2\i G
\f1\i0  might stand in for 
\f2\i Gravity
\f1\i0 .\'94\
Chip covered his eyes with his hands as his jaw went slack.\
Sarah pushed. \'93I imagine treating all those dimensions like rubber could be like throwing match into a box of fireworks.\'94\
The air came out of Chip\'92s lungs but his hands stayed affixed to his eye sockets. Eventually he could bring himself to see the corridor ahead. He waited while Sarah stretched her mind around a couple of things.\
\'93Rubber topology,\'94 she said.\
\'93What of it?\'94 Chip sounded exasperated.\
\'93The washing machine is performing\'85 what? Rubber topology in multiple dimensions?\'94\
\'93Rubber topology in 
\f2\i G
\f1\i0 .\'94\
Sarah\'92s eyes boggled. \'93In all dimensions.\'94\
\'93And even then, you can\'92t possibly understand what that means.\'94\
\'93Explain.\'94\
Chip considered the weight of the request. \'93Even thinking in dimensions is still snooker-ball physics.\'94\
\'93What should we be thinking in?\'94\
\'93We don\'92t  have the words. Even Zen Buddhists don\'92t have the un-words.\'94\
\'93That\'92s very clever, Chip, but it\'92s not helping.\'94\
\'93Think potential, or possibilities, or\'85 options.\'94\
Sarah reconstructed her thoughts and spoke slowly. \'93So, the Gyges discs spin in all the 
\f2\i options
\f1\i0 ?\'94\
\'93That\'92s about as close as we can get to it without the equations.\'94\
Sarah was experimenting with the novel notions. \'93Spin Gyges discs are a literal coin toss.\'94 \
\'93It\'92s more like tossing a coin a thousand times and getting 
\f2\i all 
\f1\i0 the results at once.\'94\
\'93Or all the consequences.\'94\
\'93Now you are getting it.\'94\
\'93And the washing machine is performing rubber topology over all the options of all the coin tosses.\'94\
\'93Actually, there\'92s where you can revert back to the D-word.\'94\
Sarah rephrased,\'93Rubber topology over all the dimensions.\'94\
\'93Yep,\'94 Chip confirmed.\
\'93So we\'92re stretching the rubber to make everything fit?\'94\
\'93Mr Stoat\'92s crude analogy aside, there are consequences of stretching the rubber that we don\'92t understand yet.\'94\
\'93The condom could break,\'94 Sarah quipped, and regretted it immediately.\
Chip look at Sarah\'92s belly bulge. \'93Unexpected things will happen.\'94 His deadpan prediction chilled Sarah.\
\'93How did we get here, Chip? How did we end up using technology that can put two places on earth    in the same space for keeping our bananas fresh?\'94\
Chip looked sideways are Sarah. \'93I think you already know the answer to that.\'94\
Sarah took her time to answer. \'93Pandora\'92s stasis box.\'94\
Chip grumbled.\
\'93Stasis technology has effectively reduced food waste to zero,\'94 Sarah said.\
Chip looked away and huffed. \'93Well, yes, but that\'92s not the point.\'94\
\'93It\'92s like any technology. You have to balance the advantages and consequences.\'94\
Chip was getting impatient. \'93Balance? There\'92s no balance. You\'92re smarter than that.\'94\
\'93Am I?\'94\
Chip still hadn\'92t made eye contact. \'93Smart enough to read the Food Preservation Secrets Act and understand what\'92s really in it.\'94
